From 3a53183a0a430b75aad41b767bf6675e60bd026b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:48:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 41/63] glm cuda: TF_GLM_ABSORB_MMA=1, a prompt's absorb_q and
 expand_v as head-batched tensor-core GEMMs (opt-in)

A prompt pass's MLA absorb_q (q . wk, [heads][256][512]) and expand_v (o_lat . wv, [heads][256][512]) run on the SIMT
fma-and-shuffle kernels at 11-13 TFLOPS. With TF_GLM_ABSORB_MMA=1, rows >= 64 run instead as one bf16 GEMM per head
with fp32 sums on tensor cores (tf_glm_latent_mma_kn: B as [K][N] through ldmatrix.trans; tf_glm_latent_mma_nk: B as
[N][K]), 128 x 128 blocks of 8 warps, K 32 a stage in three cp.async stages, one head a z. Decode windows keep the
SIMT kernels. The weights are read as stored: no transposed copy.

Measured on one RTX PRO 6000 at 2048 rows x 32 heads: absorb 1.212 -> 0.113 ms, expand 1.471 -> 0.093 ms (10.7x and
15.8x); against float64 both paths have the same rel-RMS error (the bf16 output rounding), and sampled outputs were
bit-equal to the SIMT kernels'. The fp32 summation order differs, so the flag is off by default.

The opt-in prompt numerics are a new Settings.numerics field in every rank's fingerprint (layout 13): ranks that
disagree refuse to start.

